From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: sy7758: make the enable GPIO optional

The AYANEO Pocket DS wires no discrete enable line to its SY7758, and
requiring one leaves the whole lower DSI chain deferred. Boards that do
describe the GPIO are unaffected.

---
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c
@@ -184,8 +184,11 @@
 
 	fsleep(100);
 
-	/* Get enable GPIO and set to high */
-	sydev->gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
+	/*
+	 * Some boards route SY7758 EN through a dedicated GPIO, while Pocket DS
+	 * leaves the chip reachable without a separately-described enable pin.
+	 */
+	sydev->gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
 	if (IS_ERR(sydev->gpio))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(sydev->gpio),
 				     "failed to get enable GPIO\n");
